     "about": "Page guard for the CUSTOMERS_MODULE_ENABLED module licence. Mirror of projectsModuleGuardChain — see that file for the shared rationale. Runs FIRST on vbEnter (before the page's own init). If the Customers module is off, redirects home and returns so the page never renders. This catches deep-links, bookmarks and browser history that bypass the hidden nav — hiding a menu item removes the affordance, not the route. Destination is owned by getHomeTarget(), never re-derived here. Under the one-module-off invariant, Customers being off means Projects is on, so home is the project dashboard. FAILS…",
