     "about": "oj-table fires firstSelectedRowChanged PART WAY THROUGH its own select-and-focus sequence. Navigating synchronously from here tore the page down mid-sequence, and the dying table then tried to resolve the key of a row whose data was already gone: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'key') at GetKey / _fireBeforeSelectEvent / HandleSelectionOption reported by VB as \"Fatal exception delivering binding updates\", which aborts the rest of that binding-delivery cycle. Yield one macrotask so the table finishes selecting before the route changes. Navigation behaviour is unchanged.",
